<title>BRAZIL: Brazil central bank sets weaker real trading level.</title>
<headline>Brazil central bank sets weaker real trading level.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's central bank signalled a weaker trading level for the real currency by buying dollars at 1.022 real and selling dollars at 1.027 real in a buy/sell tender in the commercial foreign exchange market, dealers said.</p>
<p>Under the previous mini-band set on September 30, the real was traded between 1.021 and 1.026 real to the dollar.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
